[{:db/id 17592186059690 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7953127-b916-5d8d-98b4-eeece8a2e1ec"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c7953127-b916-5d8d-98b4-eeece8a2e1ec" :question/id #uuid "c7953127-b916-5d8d-98b4-eeece8a2e1ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-81892" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $(¬B∧C)⇒(B∨¬C).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n(¬B∧C)⇒(B∨¬C)≡¬(¬B∧C)∨(B∨¬C).\n$$\n\nWe can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬B∧C)∨(B∨¬C)≡(¬(¬B)∨¬C)∨(B∨¬C)\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n(¬(¬B)∨¬C)∨(B∨¬C)≡(B∨¬C)∨(B∨¬C).\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the disjunction of a statement with itself:\n\n$$\n(B∨¬C)∨(B∨¬C)≡B∨¬C\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $B∨¬C.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eea492f1-156d-5834-96c0-8454fc274282"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eea492f1-156d-5834-96c0-8454fc274282" :answer-field/id #uuid "eea492f1-156d-5834-96c0-8454fc274282" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-191c421c-bbe9-5286-9beb-03027543bcc3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35dc661b-8042-5dd9-ae2c-1ddb0493316b" "answer-4c2b2d55-0e4e-5769-9706-03ec9ecc763c" "answer-191c421c-bbe9-5286-9beb-03027543bcc3" "answer-442d26c2-04f3-57d7-adf7-53465469c631" "answer-33e9615f-fd80-5202-949f-ebfef4f3e8b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35dc661b-8042-5dd9-ae2c-1ddb0493316b" :answer/id #uuid "35dc661b-8042-5dd9-ae2c-1ddb0493316b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B∧¬C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c2b2d55-0e4e-5769-9706-03ec9ecc763c" :answer/id #uuid "4c2b2d55-0e4e-5769-9706-03ec9ecc763c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B∨C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-191c421c-bbe9-5286-9beb-03027543bcc3" :answer/id #uuid "191c421c-bbe9-5286-9beb-03027543bc